WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
MkvDrama.net

00:04.504 --> 00:06.297
Oh, it's starting!

00:06.381 --> 00:07.465
Hurry!

00:12.804 --> 00:13.722
All right.

00:18.560 --> 00:20.895
Well, a lot of stuff happened,

00:20.979 --> 00:24.023
but that's the thrill
of a live broadcast, right?

00:24.107 --> 00:28.153
Thank you for staying with us
until the very end today.

00:28.737 --> 00:31.406
-Goodbye for now!
-Three, two, one…

00:32.323 --> 00:33.283
Okay!

00:34.159 --> 00:35.702
Good work, everyone!

00:35.785 --> 00:36.619
Good work!

00:36.703 --> 00:37.954
Good work!

00:38.038 --> 00:40.331
Your improvisation was amazing.

00:40.415 --> 00:43.209
-Doing this live, every time.
-It was really funny.

00:43.293 --> 00:44.419
You're a big help.

00:44.502 --> 00:45.587
Thank you.

00:45.670 --> 00:48.590
I'll see you at the party, right?
It's in your honor.

00:51.009 --> 00:52.135
Oh, excuse me.

01:04.272 --> 01:07.817
You're too intense, working on
these ideas until morning.

01:08.693 --> 01:09.944
You think so?

01:11.446 --> 01:13.865
On the very day
of the live broadcast, no less.

01:18.036 --> 01:19.454
Mr. Amagi is coming through.

01:19.537 --> 01:21.206
-Good work.
-Thank you.

01:29.506 --> 01:31.591
I'm going to go greet the staff first.

01:31.674 --> 01:32.509
Okay.

01:35.053 --> 01:36.346
See you.

01:40.683 --> 01:42.936
Make sure to show up tonight, okay?

01:44.604 --> 01:45.688
Sure.

01:48.274 --> 01:51.236
I don't know what you're thinking, but…

02:00.537 --> 02:03.081
In an era where television
is in a recession,

02:03.164 --> 02:06.084
the reason we've come this far
is thanks to the performers,

02:06.167 --> 02:07.961
the staff members,

02:08.044 --> 02:11.256
and the sponsors who support us every day.

02:11.339 --> 02:14.884
I want to take this opportunity
to thank you from the bottom of my heart.

02:14.968 --> 02:17.929
Being loved for this long
is not to be taken for granted.

02:18.012 --> 02:20.098
KOICHI AMAGI: I WANT TO TALK

02:20.181 --> 02:22.851
Let's celebrate
along with former staff members,

02:22.934 --> 02:27.438
and many familiar faces
of past performers who are here today.

02:30.859 --> 02:33.236
It doesn't look like it's going to stop.

02:34.237 --> 02:36.614
Everyone, let's move inside for now!

02:36.698 --> 02:38.658
Sorry! Follow me, please.

02:38.741 --> 02:39.576
Just here!

02:39.659 --> 02:42.662
Please be careful! It's slippery.

02:44.372 --> 02:45.290
Sorry!

02:45.999 --> 02:48.042
YUSATA 20TH ANNIVERSARY
CELEBRATION VENUE

02:58.428 --> 02:59.721
Excuse me.

02:59.804 --> 03:01.347
-Here, sorry.
-Thank you.

03:01.431 --> 03:03.182
-Thank you.
-Yes.

03:05.643 --> 03:06.561
Hey.

03:06.644 --> 03:08.855
It's the 20th anniversary of Yusata.
Isn't that amazing?

03:09.439 --> 03:11.733
-That's the one with Koichi Amagi, right?
-Yes.

03:11.816 --> 03:14.444
Twenty years ago, I was four years old.

03:15.612 --> 03:18.781
Dr. Masumi, do you ever watch television?

03:20.950 --> 03:23.494
I do not watch it frequently,

03:23.578 --> 03:25.663
but I value making time for comedy.

03:25.747 --> 03:26.873
That's surprising.

03:27.457 --> 03:32.545
Laughing secretes oxytocin,
which alleviates stress and anxiety.

03:32.629 --> 03:35.381
Therefore, I deliberately
make time for laughter.

03:35.465 --> 03:36.799
Wow.

03:36.883 --> 03:38.218
You should laugh more.

03:38.301 --> 03:39.469
Look who's talking.

03:39.552 --> 03:41.721
By the way, where is Dr. Honda?

03:41.804 --> 03:44.140
He's gone for a week
for an academic conference.

03:44.224 --> 03:45.808
That's awfully long.

03:45.892 --> 03:48.394
He seemed really
enthusiastic about it, though.

03:48.478 --> 03:51.314
Is that really just because of
the conference?

03:51.898 --> 03:52.732
Who knows?

03:52.815 --> 03:55.026
Hello, this is Medical Examiner Japan.

03:55.109 --> 03:56.736
JAPAN NEWS

03:59.405 --> 04:00.406
What?

04:01.157 --> 04:02.325
Is something wrong?

04:02.951 --> 04:04.202
Dr. Matsubara?

04:05.828 --> 04:08.122
Understood, we will
head there immediately.

04:12.877 --> 04:16.005
It says Koichi Amagi has suddenly died.

04:17.006 --> 04:18.633
KOICHI AMAGI (55) DIES SUDDENLY

04:19.634 --> 04:20.593
What?

04:29.852 --> 04:31.312
POLICE

04:34.399 --> 04:36.359
Koichi Amagi, 55-year-old male.

04:36.442 --> 04:37.777
He is believed to have jumped

04:37.860 --> 04:42.407
during the 20th anniversary celebration
of the program held at the station.

04:42.490 --> 04:44.325
The first person to discover him

04:44.409 --> 04:47.537
was Kazuhiko Muto, who serves
as the head director for Yusata.

04:47.620 --> 04:49.038
Hearing a loud noise,

04:49.122 --> 04:51.207
he went out to check the situation,

04:51.291 --> 04:54.502
found Mr. Amagi after his fall,
and reported it.

04:55.920 --> 04:57.964
Where did the fall occur from?

04:58.923 --> 05:01.092
It is believed he fell from over there.

05:04.262 --> 05:07.015
Since no suicide note
was found at the scene,

05:07.098 --> 05:09.600
it is thought that he jumped on impulse.

05:15.315 --> 05:17.358
Is something the matter, Doctor?

05:18.359 --> 05:21.195
For a jump from that height,

05:21.279 --> 05:23.281
the body is far too clean.

05:23.865 --> 05:26.075
The amount of bleeding
and external trauma is minimal.

05:27.076 --> 05:28.202
It doesn't add up.

05:28.286 --> 05:31.622
We have also received information
that he was mentally unstable.

05:46.471 --> 05:50.683
I wonder if he had some things going on
in private.

05:53.644 --> 05:57.690
YUSATA 20TH ANNIVERSARY
CELEBRATION VENUE

06:03.196 --> 06:05.114
I see.

06:06.949 --> 06:09.952
So this time MEJ is
involved with Amagi's case.

06:13.581 --> 06:14.916
That is troublesome.

06:18.461 --> 06:20.088
When it's a case involving a celebrity,

06:20.171 --> 06:22.173
we have to take into account
public opinion,

06:22.256 --> 06:23.800
making it harder for us.

06:23.883 --> 06:26.385
Has a suicide note been found
on Amagi's body?

06:26.469 --> 06:27.970
Is foul play suspected?

06:28.054 --> 06:29.305
Were there any witnesses?

06:29.388 --> 06:31.641
It was a celebration for Yusata, right?

06:31.724 --> 06:33.559
We don't know anything yet!

06:33.643 --> 06:34.560
Yes?

06:37.188 --> 06:38.147
What?

06:50.535 --> 06:51.744
Let's begin.

06:57.667 --> 07:00.503
The cause of death is traumatic shock.

07:01.003 --> 07:02.630
Abdominal internal bleeding

07:02.713 --> 07:05.758
and multiple fractures of the skull
and ribs were confirmed.

07:05.842 --> 07:07.760
Judging by the internal damage,

07:07.844 --> 07:10.430
it is certain that the body
sustained a powerful impact.

07:11.639 --> 07:14.892
But the external damage is minimal,
isn't it?

07:14.976 --> 07:19.147
Yes. This leaves room for doubt regarding
the findings of a suicide by jumping.

07:19.230 --> 07:23.234
It is as if only the interior of the body
experienced the fall.

07:23.317 --> 07:24.652
It doesn't add up.

07:24.735 --> 07:25.778
Right.

07:25.862 --> 07:29.198
Furthermore, there are numerous
linear marks on the arms and back

07:29.282 --> 07:32.493
that are not typically seen
in falls from great heights.

07:32.577 --> 07:35.163
And there is one more point of concern.

07:35.246 --> 07:36.664
What is it?

07:38.249 --> 07:42.044
A tongue bite wound located on the side.

07:42.628 --> 07:45.089
It is true that in cases of jumping,

07:45.173 --> 07:47.925
the lower jaw moves rapidly
in the closing direction,

07:48.009 --> 07:50.261
and wounds usually appear at the front.

07:50.344 --> 07:52.430
Why would it be on the side?

07:53.806 --> 07:57.477
Additionally, there are old
fracture scars on the skull.

07:58.060 --> 08:00.146
Could these be connected to something?

08:00.229 --> 08:01.731
Right now, we do not know.

08:01.814 --> 08:05.318
But it is difficult to consider this
a simple case of jumping.

08:10.781 --> 08:12.867
Why are you in such a hurry?

08:13.326 --> 08:16.913
The higher-ups are telling us
to process this as having no foul play.

08:17.997 --> 08:19.123
What?

08:24.587 --> 08:27.006
What's going on?
The police are pulling out?

08:27.089 --> 08:29.550
Looking at the circumstances,
he simply jumped.

08:29.634 --> 08:32.136
Testimony said
that he had suicidal thoughts.

08:32.220 --> 08:34.305
MEJ is currently investigating that--

08:34.388 --> 08:36.432
Looking at the circumstances,

08:37.099 --> 08:38.893
it was just a suicide.

08:50.613 --> 08:52.406
If it isn't Ms. Dojima.

08:52.949 --> 08:54.158
You look well.

09:00.665 --> 09:01.916
Please leave.

09:10.258 --> 09:11.759
It's pressure from the higher-ups,

09:11.842 --> 09:15.012
so I doubt even Ms. Dojima
can do anything about this.

09:20.518 --> 09:22.103
What should we do, Doctor?

09:44.417 --> 09:45.835
Mr. Muto,

09:45.918 --> 09:50.506
did you meet with Mr. Amagi
just before he passed away?

09:50.590 --> 09:53.342
Yes, briefly, to discuss the show.

09:53.426 --> 09:56.304
He sent me a message saying
he wanted to talk in private.

09:56.387 --> 09:57.430
I WANT TO TALK

10:02.852 --> 10:04.437
What did you want to talk about?

10:09.692 --> 10:11.736
There are many guests here today.

10:15.031 --> 10:17.450
You'll be fine even if I'm gone, right?

10:18.367 --> 10:19.285
What?

10:22.330 --> 10:23.914
I'm at my limit.

10:27.585 --> 10:29.587
It gave me a bad feeling.

10:30.254 --> 10:32.798
Had he not consulted you
about anything before that?

10:32.882 --> 10:34.008
Never.

10:34.091 --> 10:36.886
Lately, we only had routine
work-related communications,

10:36.969 --> 10:39.889
mostly handled through his wife,
who acts as his manager.

10:42.058 --> 10:45.728
He really changed. He did.

10:47.521 --> 10:50.483
Now, he's a nationwide star…

10:50.566 --> 10:51.609
Thank you.

10:51.692 --> 10:56.030
…while we're just a small production
company riding on his coattails.

10:57.365 --> 10:59.408
To him, I suppose this program

11:00.576 --> 11:03.829
was just one of many shows he was on.

11:06.624 --> 11:07.625
I'm sorry.

11:08.751 --> 11:10.628
I shouldn't have vented like this.

11:11.212 --> 11:12.338
It's okay.

11:13.506 --> 11:17.259
Do you know about Mr. Amagi
having a pre-existing medical condition?

11:17.343 --> 11:18.719
No, nothing in particular.

11:19.720 --> 11:20.930
I see.

11:26.811 --> 11:28.521
What is this?

11:29.230 --> 11:30.564
Oh.

11:30.648 --> 11:32.942
It's the broadcast records
for the past 20 years.

11:33.025 --> 11:35.027
It's for the memorial special.

11:35.111 --> 11:36.570
May I take a look at it?

11:36.654 --> 11:37.780
Go ahead.

11:41.409 --> 11:43.619
He was always doing as he pleased.

11:47.498 --> 11:49.542
What happened
during this particular month?

11:50.126 --> 11:51.043
Pardon?

11:52.211 --> 11:54.880
This is a regularly scheduled
live broadcast, correct?

11:54.964 --> 11:59.051
He suddenly demanded
an extended leave of absence.

11:59.635 --> 12:02.179
It was pretty tough
trying to fill it up with recaps.

12:04.432 --> 12:07.810
2021 JUNE 5TH - NO BROADCAST
JUNE 12-26 RECAP EPISODES

12:08.644 --> 12:09.728
Mr. Muto.

12:09.812 --> 12:10.938
Yes?

12:11.021 --> 12:12.440
What are you doing?

12:13.065 --> 12:16.318
We need you
to finish the script structure quickly.

12:16.402 --> 12:18.863
Oh, right.

12:18.946 --> 12:20.781
Sorry, we know you're busy.

12:20.865 --> 12:22.616
Thank you very much.

12:22.700 --> 12:25.870
Twenty years of consistent broadcasting
is truly impressive.

12:28.747 --> 12:31.041
The writers are waiting for you.

12:32.084 --> 12:33.544
Excuse me.

12:50.936 --> 12:54.190
Things disappear so often
at TV stations, don't they?

12:54.273 --> 12:56.817
There are always so many
people coming and going.

12:56.901 --> 12:59.487
Even a suitcase went missing recently.

12:59.570 --> 13:00.821
Excuse me.

13:02.198 --> 13:04.158
May I have one of these?

13:04.241 --> 13:05.242
What?

13:05.326 --> 13:07.244
Sliced melon is my absolute favorite.

13:08.037 --> 13:08.954
Go ahead.

13:09.038 --> 13:10.915
Thank you very much.

13:10.998 --> 13:12.291
Sorry.

13:24.762 --> 13:26.013
This is…

13:27.139 --> 13:28.390
Love-chan.

13:28.474 --> 13:29.350
LOVE-CHAN'S BIG ADVENTURE

13:31.519 --> 13:34.021
I adore this character.

13:36.398 --> 13:37.399
Love-chan.

13:46.408 --> 13:48.577
AMAGI

13:48.661 --> 13:54.375
Did Mr. Amagi ever seem troubled
or stressed about his work?

13:54.875 --> 13:56.585
No, not particularly.

13:59.838 --> 14:03.259
Were you also present at the venue
on that day?

14:05.886 --> 14:08.597
Did he keep his plans
in a schedule or anything?

14:08.681 --> 14:10.266
Oh, yes.

14:10.808 --> 14:12.184
May we take a look at it?

14:14.311 --> 14:15.354
Sure.

14:21.777 --> 14:22.695
Here you go.

14:22.778 --> 14:24.113
Thank you very much.

14:33.789 --> 14:37.084
He was an extraordinarily
meticulous person, wasn't he?

14:37.585 --> 14:40.629
He broke his schedule down
into 30-minute blocks.

14:41.380 --> 14:44.633
He disciplined himself strictly
to prepare for the live broadcasts.

14:47.428 --> 14:50.514
Running, yoga, even reading.

14:55.102 --> 14:57.605
What's this time written in red?

14:58.731 --> 14:59.732
What?

15:01.066 --> 15:02.109
This.

15:07.197 --> 15:10.284
I believe my husband
was simply keeping a record

15:10.367 --> 15:12.286
of the days he couldn't finish on time.

15:14.204 --> 15:16.248
He was a man of very particular habits.

15:21.587 --> 15:23.130
I see.

15:23.881 --> 15:26.967
Thank you for speaking with us
during such a difficult time.

15:32.264 --> 15:35.309
To think he managed his life
with that much stoicism…

15:37.645 --> 15:40.064
Living life in 30-minute increments…

15:42.274 --> 15:44.944
It must have been difficult
for Yuka as well.

15:49.865 --> 15:54.620
He may have had a side to him
that he never showed to anyone.

16:23.482 --> 16:26.610
TAKASAKA FAMILY GRAVE

16:39.832 --> 16:42.584
INCOMING CALL

16:47.047 --> 16:49.049
PRIVATE CALLER

16:59.143 --> 17:00.185
I'm back.

17:01.645 --> 17:06.150
Regarding Mr. Amagi,
no poison was detected in the body.

17:06.233 --> 17:07.901
Really?

17:09.611 --> 17:10.779
Thank you.

17:12.239 --> 17:13.866
I'm back.

17:16.577 --> 17:18.370
What are you looking at?

17:18.454 --> 17:20.539
Surveillance camera footage from that day.

17:20.622 --> 17:23.667
Igawa gave it to us, hoping
it might help with the investigation.

17:24.501 --> 17:25.544
Excuse me.

17:27.421 --> 17:31.467
ROOF CAMERA

17:32.551 --> 17:36.680
I believe Mr. Muto discovers
his friend's body shortly after this.

17:36.764 --> 17:39.349
Could you show me that one more time?

17:39.433 --> 17:40.309
Yes.

17:50.152 --> 17:52.905
YUSATA'S 20TH ANNIVERSARY CELEBRATION

18:02.831 --> 18:04.041
Is something wrong?

18:08.921 --> 18:11.465
Hello, this is Medical Examiner Japan.

18:11.548 --> 18:13.092
Hello, this is Igawa.

18:13.634 --> 18:17.429
Oh. Thank you for the surveillance
camera footage earlier--

18:18.764 --> 18:19.598
What?

18:20.808 --> 18:23.811
Yuka attempted suicide?

18:25.938 --> 18:27.064
What?

18:30.692 --> 18:34.863
She survived,
but she hasn't regained consciousness yet.

18:38.992 --> 18:40.285
I understand.

18:41.620 --> 18:43.122
Thank you very much.

18:48.794 --> 18:51.547
They said she overdosed on sleeping pills.

18:56.927 --> 18:58.220
Dr. Masumi.

18:58.887 --> 19:01.223
Regarding the skull fracture marks
you asked about,

19:01.306 --> 19:03.642
we found out they are
from over five years ago.

19:05.561 --> 19:08.522
MEDICAL REPORT
KOICHI AMAGI

19:08.605 --> 19:11.984
Could this have something to do
with the case?

19:12.484 --> 19:13.360
Dr. Takamori.

19:13.443 --> 19:17.739
Could you check if anything has
gone missing inside the station recently?

19:18.574 --> 19:19.491
Yes.

19:24.538 --> 19:27.082
OVERVIEW

19:31.170 --> 19:35.215
I would like to talk to you about
the long-term leave from five years ago.

19:35.299 --> 19:37.259
Is this about Amagi again?

19:37.968 --> 19:39.887
Mr. Amagi's skull had fracture marks

19:39.970 --> 19:43.724
believed to have occurred
about five years ago.

19:45.642 --> 19:48.478
Is there anything at all
you might have noticed?

19:49.062 --> 19:51.899
Maybe in the past I would have,
but not recently, no.

19:53.609 --> 19:56.028
These days he wouldn't even
show up for meetings,

19:56.111 --> 19:58.363
and when he did,
he was always checking the time.

20:00.449 --> 20:01.491
There was a time

20:01.575 --> 20:04.578
when he cared about the program
more than anyone, though.

20:06.163 --> 20:08.373
How about this for the next segment?

20:08.457 --> 20:10.959
Really? You brought another one?

20:13.337 --> 20:15.130
Sorry, but I'm busy.

20:25.849 --> 20:27.017
Excuse me.

20:29.937 --> 20:32.981
Didn't we meet
in the editing room the other day?

20:33.482 --> 20:34.524
Right.

20:35.692 --> 20:39.696
There is a possibility that the period
when Mr. Amagi took his long-term leave

20:39.780 --> 20:42.741
matches the timing
of the fracture found on his skull.

20:44.868 --> 20:48.121
Do you happen to know anything about it?

20:53.919 --> 20:56.338
I thought I would have
to tell someone eventually.

20:57.923 --> 20:59.466
Five years ago,

21:00.467 --> 21:02.719
I was the one
who caused Mr. Amagi's injury.

21:04.930 --> 21:05.973
What?

21:06.556 --> 21:07.724
Back then,

21:07.808 --> 21:10.102
I was still just a new director.

21:10.185 --> 21:12.187
I was working for days, without sleeping.

21:13.563 --> 21:15.065
I was totally out of it.

21:24.574 --> 21:25.867
I'm sorry!

21:26.451 --> 21:27.577
I'm fine.

21:27.661 --> 21:29.037
No, but…

21:29.121 --> 21:30.831
-What happened?
-I'm really fine.

21:30.914 --> 21:32.207
I'm sorry, I was careless…

21:32.291 --> 21:33.792
-You okay?
-Don't worry!

21:33.875 --> 21:35.085
Don't worry.

21:37.504 --> 21:39.464
A light just tipped over.

21:45.304 --> 21:48.390
At the time, our ratings were stagnant,

21:49.099 --> 21:52.311
and the show was
on the chopping block for cancellation.

21:53.645 --> 21:54.646
So,

21:55.480 --> 21:57.107
we kept it a secret.

21:59.818 --> 22:04.197
So the fracture marks on his head
were caused by that accident.

22:04.781 --> 22:05.782
Yes.

22:05.866 --> 22:09.286
Did Mr. Muto really not know about it?

22:10.495 --> 22:12.873
I don't think he knew about the fracture.

22:15.292 --> 22:16.626
I see.

22:21.173 --> 22:26.803
So the skull fracture marks
were from an accident that was covered up.

22:31.058 --> 22:31.975
Hello?

22:33.894 --> 22:35.062
What?

22:35.145 --> 22:36.104
Really?

22:38.065 --> 22:39.941
Yuka has regained consciousness.

22:41.318 --> 22:42.736
I will go check on her.

22:42.819 --> 22:43.820
Okay.

22:43.904 --> 22:45.322
I will stay here a little longer.

22:45.405 --> 22:46.406
Right, okay.

22:47.407 --> 22:49.409
May I come visit now?

22:55.457 --> 22:56.541
Excuse me.

22:56.625 --> 22:59.586
I am Masumi
from the Medical Examiner's office.

22:59.669 --> 23:00.712
Yes?

23:00.796 --> 23:04.466
Did Mr. Amagi come here often?

23:05.050 --> 23:06.009
Yes.

23:06.093 --> 23:10.055
Ever since Yusata started, he has always
stopped by before the live broadcast.

23:10.931 --> 23:12.516
Around what time would that be?

23:12.599 --> 23:16.686
He would come to get water
30 minutes before the broadcast.

23:17.354 --> 23:20.941
I guess even a star gets nervous
before a live broadcast, right?

23:21.483 --> 23:25.570
Especially him, since he cared about
his routine more than anyone.

23:37.082 --> 23:41.044
I'm sorry for suddenly
asking so many questions

23:41.128 --> 23:45.090
when we visited the other day.

23:49.803 --> 23:52.472
I'm glad you are safe.

24:02.858 --> 24:07.737
I used to watch Mr. Amagi's show
often at this time.

24:09.573 --> 24:13.076
He always looked so happy on screen.

24:15.328 --> 24:17.873
When I watched him,

24:18.832 --> 24:22.502
it made the fatigue of the week
melt away a little.

24:28.884 --> 24:29.718
But,

24:31.303 --> 24:32.554
I think…

24:34.723 --> 24:36.933
he had many hardships going on

24:40.270 --> 24:45.192
that we as viewers never knew about.

24:50.822 --> 24:52.115
And I think that,

24:53.241 --> 24:54.910
for decades,

24:56.453 --> 24:59.206
he was able to give so much joy to people…

25:02.375 --> 25:04.794
because you were there for him.

25:10.800 --> 25:11.760
Actually…

25:18.516 --> 25:20.060
Sorry to call you.

25:21.019 --> 25:22.854
Regarding MEJ,

25:23.355 --> 25:26.650
you know how the prosecution
feels about them, right?

25:26.733 --> 25:27.609
MINISTRY OF HEALTH, LABOR AND WELFARE

25:27.692 --> 25:31.404
I understand. I will have someone
look into the internal affairs of MEJ.

25:33.657 --> 25:36.868
You truly are a smart person,
Mr. Yamazaki.

25:38.912 --> 25:39.746
Okay.

25:40.956 --> 25:43.625
I will report back as soon as I find out.

26:02.769 --> 26:04.896
Is that from the anniversary celebration?

26:04.980 --> 26:06.147
Oh, yes.

26:07.774 --> 26:09.150
What video is that?

26:09.859 --> 26:11.778
Live stream footage from the party.

26:11.861 --> 26:14.322
We're at the Yusata party!

26:15.115 --> 26:19.327
It hurts to think that at this time,
he might have died already.

26:20.120 --> 26:23.415
"Is Mr. Amagi there, too?"

26:28.128 --> 26:29.254
Dr. Masumi.

26:29.337 --> 26:31.214
I received this from Yuka.

26:32.590 --> 26:33.883
INTERNAL MEDICINE
KOICHI AMAGI

26:37.512 --> 26:40.432
Dr. Takamori, do you have
the station's lost and found list?

26:43.810 --> 26:45.145
Here it is.

26:50.400 --> 26:52.235
LIGHT BLUE SUITCASE

27:00.869 --> 27:03.038
It is believed he fell from over there.

27:03.121 --> 27:05.540
There are numerous linear marks…

27:05.623 --> 27:07.000
…bite wound.

27:07.584 --> 27:10.503
He broke his schedule down
into 30-minute blocks.

27:10.587 --> 27:12.589
What's this time written in red?

27:12.672 --> 27:14.257
My husband was simply keeping a record

27:14.341 --> 27:16.009
of the days he couldn't finish on time.

27:16.092 --> 27:17.761
He was always just checking the time.

27:19.137 --> 27:22.557
He would come to get water
30 minutes before the broadcast.

27:22.640 --> 27:23.933
Five years ago,

27:24.017 --> 27:26.061
I was the one
who caused Mr. Amagi's injury.

27:26.144 --> 27:28.646
I don't think he knew about the fracture.

27:30.357 --> 27:32.984
Things disappear so often
at TV stations, don't they?

27:33.068 --> 27:36.112
Even a suitcase went missing recently.

27:36.196 --> 27:39.574
I believe Mr. Muto discovers
his friend's body shortly after this.

27:41.951 --> 27:45.497
It is as if only the interior of the body
experienced the fall.

27:59.469 --> 28:00.970
The pieces may be…

28:02.180 --> 28:03.973
coming together.

28:07.811 --> 28:11.147
INTERNAL MEDICINE
KOICHI AMAGI

28:26.079 --> 28:28.915
Oh. I'm sorry.
I know you're busy, Mr. Muto.

28:29.499 --> 28:31.668
What did you want to talk about?

28:31.751 --> 28:35.755
According to the autopsy,
the cause of Mr. Amagi's death

28:35.839 --> 28:39.467
was traumatic shock
from a fall from a high place.

28:40.969 --> 28:41.886
However,

28:41.970 --> 28:46.015
what struck me as highly unusual
was how clean the body was.

28:48.893 --> 28:54.607
There were far too few external injuries
for a fall from such a height.

28:54.691 --> 28:57.819
It was almost as if
he was being protected by something.

29:00.196 --> 29:01.406
Furthermore,

29:01.489 --> 29:05.326
Mr. Amagi's body had linear abrasions

29:05.410 --> 29:08.580
that could not have been
caused by jumping.

29:10.373 --> 29:11.541
Linear abrasions?

29:11.624 --> 29:12.625
Yes.

29:14.043 --> 29:18.631
The kind you get when rolling down
a flight of stairs, for instance.

29:20.759 --> 29:21.885
In other words,

29:21.968 --> 29:25.430
Amagi was involved in a separate incident

29:25.513 --> 29:28.850
before his fall from a higher location.

29:37.192 --> 29:39.611
You'll be fine even if I'm gone, right?

29:40.528 --> 29:41.446
What?

29:44.532 --> 29:46.075
I'm at my limit.

29:52.165 --> 29:54.042
If that's a joke, it's not funny.

30:01.591 --> 30:03.927
Why now, of all times?

30:12.060 --> 30:13.228
What's the reason?

30:21.152 --> 30:22.237
Fine.

30:23.655 --> 30:24.906
Let's go somewhere else.

30:27.700 --> 30:28.576
Hey!

30:28.660 --> 30:30.787
YUSATA 20TH ANNIVERSARY
CELEBRATION VENUE

30:30.870 --> 30:31.788
Hey.

30:31.871 --> 30:33.748
You just got tired of it, didn't you?

30:34.958 --> 30:36.501
Must be nice for you.

30:37.335 --> 30:40.588
You'll have plenty of work
even if Yusata gets canceled.

30:43.967 --> 30:46.010
Just because you got a little famous…

30:49.055 --> 30:50.640
Say something.

30:51.641 --> 30:52.934
Whoa, hey!

30:56.229 --> 30:58.773
Hey!

30:58.857 --> 31:00.692
Hey!

31:05.697 --> 31:08.032
H-He's dead…

31:08.116 --> 31:09.993
Because those linear abrasions

31:10.076 --> 31:13.413
were not present
during the evening live broadcast,

31:13.997 --> 31:17.834
we believe they were sustained
during the celebration party.

31:20.044 --> 31:22.422
You were the first to find him,

31:22.505 --> 31:26.759
and we were told you rushed over
immediately upon hearing a sound.

31:27.635 --> 31:31.389
While your actions
were captured on security footage,

31:31.472 --> 31:35.018
the direction you headed raises questions.

31:37.312 --> 31:39.480
Why did you go out of your way
to take a detour

31:39.564 --> 31:41.816
to reach the spot where he fell?

31:42.442 --> 31:43.318
That's because--

31:43.401 --> 31:46.529
If you truly rushed over
the moment you heard the sound,

31:47.155 --> 31:49.407
then this behavior

31:50.158 --> 31:51.534
doesn't add up.

31:53.453 --> 31:55.955
Everyone, let's move inside for now!

31:56.039 --> 31:57.999
Sorry, follow me please!

31:59.334 --> 32:01.461
Please be careful! It's slippery.

32:03.963 --> 32:04.797
Excuse me!

32:05.798 --> 32:06.925
I'm very sorry!

32:15.266 --> 32:20.521
A large suitcase has gone missing
from this television station.

32:20.605 --> 32:23.691
Even a suitcase went missing recently.

32:23.775 --> 32:28.321
Given that the celebration party
was underway that day,

32:28.821 --> 32:30.865
you hid Mr. Amagi

32:31.824 --> 32:33.451
inside that suitcase

32:34.827 --> 32:38.581
to keep him out of sight, didn't you?

32:44.212 --> 32:47.632
The missing suitcase
can actually be spotted

32:47.715 --> 32:50.635
in a video that was being
live-streamed during the party.

32:51.469 --> 32:52.345
For some reason,

32:52.929 --> 32:56.516
you are seen in it
pushing the suitcase in from outside.

33:00.186 --> 33:01.521
Furthermore,

33:01.604 --> 33:05.400
there's a mark on the ground that only
something angular could have made.

33:06.818 --> 33:09.362
When you put all those pieces together,

33:09.946 --> 33:14.826
it appears Amagi fell
while he was still inside that suitcase.

33:16.327 --> 33:18.287
Doesn't it seem that way?

33:27.463 --> 33:29.590
I never intended to kill him.

33:31.426 --> 33:32.510
I only tried

33:33.219 --> 33:36.597
to make him turn around on the stairs.

33:38.057 --> 33:39.183
But then,

33:40.977 --> 33:42.395
he just collapsed so easily.

33:47.233 --> 33:49.610
And the suitcase, too…

33:54.615 --> 33:56.534
I didn't intentionally drop it.

33:57.577 --> 33:59.078
It moved on its own.

33:59.162 --> 34:02.832
Mr. Amagi's hands showed absolutely
no signs of defensive wounds.

34:04.167 --> 34:05.084
What?

34:05.168 --> 34:08.004
This indicates that
he fell down the stairs

34:08.087 --> 34:11.632
without being able
to reflexively break his fall.

34:16.345 --> 34:22.351
We believe he was experiencing
a specific medical episode at that moment.

34:23.478 --> 34:26.147
One that leaves bite marks
on the side of the tongue.

34:26.230 --> 34:27.190
It was…

34:28.858 --> 34:30.151
epilepsy.

34:31.944 --> 34:33.029
Epilepsy?

34:35.031 --> 34:36.616
Must be nice for you.

34:37.408 --> 34:40.536
You'll have plenty of work
even if Yusata gets canceled.

34:47.627 --> 34:49.587
Traumatic epilepsy.

34:50.922 --> 34:52.423
It is a chronic condition

34:52.507 --> 34:55.760
that manifests when the brain
is damaged from a prior head injury.

34:56.469 --> 34:59.430
Mr. Amagi had been suffering
from traumatic epilepsy

34:59.514 --> 35:02.183
ever since an accident five years ago.

35:05.019 --> 35:09.065
This is the anti-epileptic medication
he was taking.

35:11.442 --> 35:15.530
The reason the suitcase moved
on its own on the roof is likely

35:15.613 --> 35:22.370
because Mr. Amagi regained consciousness
from his epileptic seizure.

35:42.515 --> 35:43.891
What the…

35:45.059 --> 35:48.229
Ever since that original accident,

35:48.312 --> 35:51.190
he apparently kept track of time
meticulously

35:51.274 --> 35:55.278
solely to manage his seizure patterns
and his response plan.

36:00.408 --> 36:01.742
What is all this about?

36:01.826 --> 36:03.244
I believe Mr. Amagi

36:04.120 --> 36:06.289
wanted to keep it a secret.

36:07.081 --> 36:09.333
So that you would never find out.

36:11.210 --> 36:12.211
What?

36:12.712 --> 36:16.674
INTERNAL MEDICINE
KOICHI AMAGI

36:16.757 --> 36:18.050
Five years ago,

36:19.594 --> 36:21.888
my husband developed epilepsy

36:23.347 --> 36:25.349
as the result of an accident.

36:28.269 --> 36:30.396
He made it a rule to take his medicine

36:30.479 --> 36:33.733
30 minutes before going on air,
almost like a protective ritual.

36:38.446 --> 36:39.739
I see.

36:43.701 --> 36:46.662
But why keep it a secret between you two?

36:49.624 --> 36:53.586
Couldn't he have leaned
on other people for help?

36:56.297 --> 36:59.258
My husband insisted on doing it that way.

37:01.594 --> 37:03.930
He said if his epilepsy
became public knowledge,

37:04.013 --> 37:06.057
people would dig into the root cause,

37:07.642 --> 37:10.645
and that could lead to
an investigation of the show itself.

37:12.396 --> 37:15.441
Don't you think it's time you retired?

37:16.734 --> 37:19.320
Your seizures have been
getting more frequent lately,

37:19.403 --> 37:21.030
and your body is at its limit.

37:23.324 --> 37:24.700
Just a little longer.

37:25.910 --> 37:26.786
But…

37:26.869 --> 37:28.204
Twenty years.

37:30.081 --> 37:33.376
I really want to make sure Muto
gets his moment in the spotlight.

37:35.962 --> 37:39.840
We built this show together from the days
when we were complete nobodies.

37:41.259 --> 37:42.677
This is a critical time.

37:44.011 --> 37:46.847
We live in an era
where shows get canceled easily,

37:46.931 --> 37:49.558
and everyone is working so hard
to turn things around.

37:52.561 --> 37:54.814
I know I'm asking a lot of you, but…

38:08.619 --> 38:11.414
The reason he distanced himself
from the production

38:11.497 --> 38:14.041
and was always obsessing over the time

38:16.085 --> 38:20.047
was to protect the show that held so many
special memories for you both.

38:23.217 --> 38:26.137
Even then, why…?

38:28.264 --> 38:30.850
Likely because if you knew
about his illness

38:31.684 --> 38:34.478
he thought you'd put an end to the show.

38:38.482 --> 38:41.736
You are a deeply responsible person,

38:41.819 --> 38:45.781
and Mr. Amagi knew that
better than anyone, after all.

38:49.577 --> 38:52.955
You're too intense, working on
these ideas until morning.

38:53.956 --> 38:56.375
On the very day
of the live broadcast, no less.

39:01.088 --> 39:03.299
His wife said
that right up until his death,

39:04.050 --> 39:07.762
he talked about nothing but you
whenever he was at home.

39:11.974 --> 39:15.853
That's because you waste
way too much time chatting.

39:17.313 --> 39:19.357
And you always make it worse.

39:19.982 --> 39:23.986
-How about this for the next segment?
-Really? You brought another one?

39:24.487 --> 39:25.821
You don't quit.

39:27.073 --> 39:28.074
What do you think?

39:29.575 --> 39:30.576
It's great.

39:31.077 --> 39:32.578
-Isn't it?
-Yeah.

39:36.540 --> 39:40.836
YUSATA SEGMENT IDEAS

39:49.804 --> 39:53.891
The reason he hid his illness
until he passed away

39:54.767 --> 39:56.894
was to protect the time he spent with you,

39:57.603 --> 40:01.649
which was more important
than anything else.

40:04.860 --> 40:10.533
I hope we can continue this show forever.

41:50.925 --> 41:55.179
20 YEARS OF GOODBYES ARE
A "THANK YOU" SPOKEN WITH LOVE

42:00.476 --> 42:01.894
I'm finished!

42:04.855 --> 42:05.731
Hey!

42:05.814 --> 42:07.024
Look, look!

42:07.691 --> 42:09.109
What happened?

42:11.028 --> 42:11.904
This is…

42:12.488 --> 42:14.448
I'm Suzuki from Orient Daily.

42:14.532 --> 42:17.743
Could you tell us what
has come to light during this case?

42:19.370 --> 42:21.872
They're saying MEJ probed into the truth.

42:21.956 --> 42:23.666
That makes me feel kind of proud.

42:23.749 --> 42:27.294
It's rare for forensic scientists
to get this much attention.

42:28.629 --> 42:30.339
Wow, that's amazing.

42:30.422 --> 42:32.466
Cool, huh?

42:32.550 --> 42:34.093
I'm back.

42:34.176 --> 42:35.886
-Hey!
-Welcome back!

42:35.970 --> 42:38.222
I'm back and I brought souvenirs.

42:38.305 --> 42:39.181
Oh, thank you.

42:39.265 --> 42:40.182
Thanks.

42:40.266 --> 42:41.267
Thank you.

42:42.101 --> 42:43.227
Dr. Masumi.

42:43.310 --> 42:44.186
Here.

42:44.270 --> 42:45.604
Your souvenir.

42:45.688 --> 42:46.897
LIMITED KYOTO EDITION

42:46.981 --> 42:48.482
Thank you very much.

42:49.358 --> 42:50.651
Welcome back.

42:52.861 --> 42:54.029
Thank you.

42:55.114 --> 42:58.117
-Hey, look at this, Dr. Masumi.
-What?

42:58.200 --> 43:00.244
MEJ is getting attention!

43:17.303 --> 43:18.637
ANOTHER STRANGLED BODY FOUND IN SHIRAMINE

43:18.721 --> 43:19.763
THE CITY IS ON ALERT

43:19.847 --> 43:21.515
GUARD SENT AROUND SHIRAMINE

43:31.066 --> 43:35.154
I believe many people have learned about
MEJ for the first time through this event,

43:35.237 --> 43:37.615
but could you explain once again
what kind of system it is?

43:37.698 --> 43:40.618
What was the deciding factor
in uncovering the truth?

43:43.078 --> 43:47.082
The American system has been implemented,
but have you felt any resistance?

43:52.796 --> 43:55.924
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.

43:55.924 --> 43:56.924
MkvDrama.net
